---
# Path-scoped rule: loads only when Claude works on files matching `paths`, so it costs
# nothing elsewhere. Every *.md under .claude/rules/ is picked up (recursively); this file
# ends in .example so it stays inactive. Copy it to e.g. .claude/rules/api.md, set the
# globs, and keep only what Claude can't infer from the code. A rule without `paths`
# loads in every session, like CLAUDE.md.
# Docs: https://code.claude.com/docs/en/memory#path-specific-rules
paths:
  - "src/api/**/*.ts"
---
- Validate request bodies with the schemas in src/api/schemas/; don't hand-roll checks.
- Every new endpoint needs an entry in openapi.yaml — CI fails without it.
